1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,109
Every Orchard Core site keeps its name, its time zone, and the number

2
00:00:05,109 --> 00:00:07,738
of items an admin list shows in one place:

3
00:00:07,738 --> 00:00:09,217
the General settings.

4
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:13,600
In this video, we'll open that page and go through what each setting does.

5
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:22,359
Site settings are one set of options that apply to the whole site.

6
00:00:22,359 --> 00:00:26,576
They include the site name, the default time zone, the page size of

7
00:00:26,576 --> 00:00:30,850
lists in the admin, and how scripts, stylesheets, and caches behave.

8
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,405
You find them in the admin menu under Settings, General.

9
00:00:35,405 --> 00:00:37,246
The page has three tabs:

10
00:00:37,246 --> 00:00:39,271
Site, Resources, and Cache.

11
00:00:39,271 --> 00:00:42,830
Other modules add pages of their own under Settings.

12
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,790
The page needs the Manage general settings permission.

13
00:00:46,790 --> 00:00:51,980
The Manage settings permission includes it, and the Administrator role has both by default.

14
00:00:56,171 --> 00:01:00,251
In the admin menu, let's open Settings and choose General.

15
00:01:00,714 --> 00:01:02,660
The page is titled Settings.

16
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:06,782
A warning at the top says the website might restart when you save,

17
00:01:06,782 --> 00:01:09,644
which can make it unresponsive for a moment.

18
00:01:10,097 --> 00:01:12,787
The fields are grouped in three tabs:

19
00:01:12,787 --> 00:01:14,852
Site, Resources, and Cache.

20
00:01:14,852 --> 00:01:19,357
A single Save button at the bottom saves the changes of all three.

21
00:01:23,570 --> 00:01:26,729
On the Site tab, Site name is the name that the admin and

22
00:01:26,729 --> 00:01:28,484
the themes show for the site.

23
00:01:28,484 --> 00:01:30,890
Let's replace it with Harbor Lane Journal.

24
00:01:31,346 --> 00:01:35,214
Page title format sets how the Blog theme, the theme of this site,

25
00:01:35,214 --> 00:01:37,471
builds the title of the browser tab.

26
00:01:37,471 --> 00:01:41,715
A site starts with a format that adds the site name after the page title.

27
00:01:41,715 --> 00:01:43,326
Let's leave it as it is.

28
00:01:43,781 --> 00:01:46,579
Base url is the full address of the site.

29
00:01:46,579 --> 00:01:51,163
A background task runs on its own, without a visitor's request, so when

30
00:01:51,163 --> 00:01:54,794
Base url is set, the site uses it as the address there.

31
00:01:54,794 --> 00:01:56,401
Let's leave it empty.

32
00:01:56,865 --> 00:01:57,791
Let's save.

33
00:01:57,791 --> 00:02:02,255
A message reads, Site settings updated successfully, and the name in the top

34
00:02:02,255 --> 00:02:05,195
bar of the admin changes to Harbor Lane Journal.

35
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:09,428
The Visit Site icon opens the front end, the public side of the

36
00:02:09,428 --> 00:02:13,579
site, where the Blog theme shows the same name at the top of the page.

37
00:02:17,784 --> 00:02:21,764
Default Time Zone, also on the Site tab, is the time zone the

38
00:02:21,764 --> 00:02:24,852
site uses to display and edit dates and times.

39
00:02:24,852 --> 00:02:29,544
Daylight saving time is applied automatically for the zones that have it.

40
00:02:29,999 --> 00:02:34,424
Each entry shows a time zone's name, its standard offset from GMT, and

41
00:02:34,424 --> 00:02:39,023
a second offset that includes daylight saving time while it is in effect.

42
00:02:39,023 --> 00:02:43,389
Local to server uses the time zone of the machine that runs the site.

43
00:02:43,853 --> 00:02:46,157
Let's choose Europe/London and save.

44
00:02:46,157 --> 00:02:50,163
The drop-down list shows the entry for that zone, with its offsets.

45
00:02:50,618 --> 00:02:54,310
A time zone set on a user, when the User Time Zone feature

46
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:58,058
is enabled, takes priority over this default for that user.

47
00:03:02,269 --> 00:03:07,398
This is the Manage Content page, which the Content Items menu entry opens.

48
00:03:07,398 --> 00:03:11,629
It shows one page of items, and the pager leads to the rest.

49
00:03:12,098 --> 00:03:16,780
Back in Settings, General, Page size is the default number of items on

50
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,320
one page of a list.

51
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,353
Let's set it to 5 and save.

52
00:03:20,353 --> 00:03:24,110
A page size below 1 is refused, and so is one above the

53
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:26,328
maximum page size of the site.

54
00:03:26,781 --> 00:03:32,231
Back on the list, each page holds 5 items, and the pager shows more pages.

55
00:03:32,693 --> 00:03:38,722
Back in Settings, General, Page size selection lets users choose a page size themselves.

56
00:03:38,722 --> 00:03:43,277
Let's check Allow users to change the page size on listing pages.

57
00:03:43,277 --> 00:03:45,843
A Page size options field appears.

58
00:03:46,303 --> 00:03:49,087
Let's enter 25, 5, 10 and save.

59
00:03:49,087 --> 00:03:53,301
Page size options comes back sorted, as 5, 10, 25.

60
00:03:53,301 --> 00:03:56,913
These are the sizes users can choose from.

61
00:03:57,367 --> 00:04:01,935
Back on the list, an Items per page selector sits next to the pager.

62
00:04:01,935 --> 00:04:06,317
Let's choose 10, and the list reloads with 10 items on each page.

63
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:14,347
The Resources tab has settings for scripts and stylesheets.

64
00:04:14,347 --> 00:04:19,351
Use resources cache busting appends a version to the addresses of local scripts

65
00:04:19,351 --> 00:04:22,530
and stylesheets, so browsers load changed files.

66
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:24,060
It is on by default.

67
00:04:24,513 --> 00:04:31,109
Use framework CDN (Content Delivery Network) loads registered scripts and stylesheets, such as

68
00:04:31,109 --> 00:04:34,473
jQuery, from a CDN instead of the local copy.

69
00:04:34,939 --> 00:04:40,314
Site CDN (Content Delivery Network) base url is a CDN address that prefixes

70
00:04:40,314 --> 00:04:42,703
local scripts and stylesheets.

71
00:04:42,703 --> 00:04:47,879
It is not applied while Resource Debug Mode, described next, is enabled.

72
00:04:48,341 --> 00:04:54,352
Resource Debug Mode chooses between debuggable and minified versions of scripts and stylesheets.

73
00:04:54,352 --> 00:04:59,361
The default, From environment, is disabled in Production and enabled otherwise.

74
00:04:59,832 --> 00:05:05,396
On the Cache tab, Cache Mode determines whether the dynamic caches are enabled or disabled.

75
00:05:05,396 --> 00:05:10,272
The default, From environment, is enabled in Production and disabled otherwise.

76
00:05:10,272 --> 00:05:12,452
Let's leave both tabs unchanged.

77
00:05:14,452 --> 00:05:16,782
That is the General settings page:

78
00:05:16,782 --> 00:05:21,151
the site name, the default time zone, the page size, and how scripts,

79
00:05:21,151 --> 00:05:23,307
stylesheets, and caches behave.

80
00:05:23,307 --> 00:05:24,822
Thanks for watching.

